# Forensic Investigation Report — Claude Google OAuth Compatibility

## Executive Summary
A forensic investigation was conducted into why clicking **"Continue with Google"** on `https://claude.ai/login` does nothing, while Google Accounts, ChatGPT, and GitHub OAuth work normally.

Through runtime event tracing, JavaScript console logging, and `QWebEnginePage` method instrumentation, we have **identified the exact failing component and root cause**.

Per your instructions, **no speculative code changes have been made**.

---

## 1. Investigation Findings (In Required Order)

### Item 1: `QWebEnginePage.createWindow()` Implementation
- `QWebEnginePage.createWindow()` was **not invoked** when clicking "Continue with Google".
- **Reason**: Claude.ai does not open a standard popup window (`window.open()`) or `target="_blank"` link for Google Sign-In. It uses the **Google Identity Services (GSI) JavaScript SDK** (`https://accounts.google.com/gsi/client`).

### Item 2: Event Invocations (`createWindow`, `newWindowRequested`, `acceptNavigationRequest`)
- `createWindow()`: `0` calls.
- `newWindowRequested`: `0` emissions.
- `acceptNavigationRequest()`: Navigated to `https://claude.ai/login`, loaded `https://newassets.hcaptcha.com/captcha/...`, loaded `https://accounts.google.com/gsi/client`. No navigation request was generated when clicking the button.

